# tmux AI usage: refresh interval configuration
#
# Copy this file to one of the following locations (checked in this order) and
# uncomment what you need. It is sourced as a shell fragment.
#
#   ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/tmux-usage/config
#   <this directory>/tmux-usage.conf
#
# Or point TMUX_USAGE_CONFIG at an explicit path. Environment variables of the
# same name always take precedence over this file, e.g.
#
#   TMUX_USAGE_REFRESH_SECONDS=300 ./tmux-claude-refresh.sh
#
# How stale a cached metric may get before a background refresh is triggered.
# Applies to every provider. Default: 120 seconds.
#TMUX_USAGE_REFRESH_SECONDS=120

# Optional per-provider overrides; each wins over the shared value above.
#TMUX_USAGE_CLAUDE_REFRESH_SECONDS=120
#TMUX_USAGE_OPENAI_REFRESH_SECONDS=120
#
# Notes:
#   - This is the API poll interval, not the status-line redraw interval. The
#     redraw cadence is `set -g status-interval` in tmux.conf (currently 10s)
#     and never performs network I/O.
#   - Both usage endpoints are undocumented and rate-limit hard. After a 429
#     both providers freeze fetching for 15 minutes regardless of this setting.
#   - Non-numeric or non-positive values are ignored in favour of the default.
